{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.exists_real_root_Qy_of_utilde_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.exists_real_root_Qy_of_utilde_sq","kind":"theorem","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L348-L357","doc":"**Unconditional real root of `Q` of the required shape.** There is a real `t`\nin `(2.16108, 2.16109)` with `P_t(t) = 0`, `Q(ũ(t)²) = 0`, and `0.1427 < ũ(t) < 0.1429`\n— i.e. the degree-12 polynomial `Q` of the audit genuinely annihilates the square of a\nvalue of `ũ`, and that value is the audit's `ρ` to four digits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L322-L346","doc":"**Numerical bracket on the radius candidate.** For any `t ∈ (2.16108, 2.16109)` —\nin particular for the root `t*` of `P_t` located above — `0.1427 < ũ(t) < 0.1429`.\nNumerically `ρ = ũ(t*) = 0.14279999664468968890…`. The bracket places this value\nstrictly below every other entry of the `|ũ|` singularity inventory (next-nearest\n`0.2575`; the fold at `0.4502`), which is what makes it the *dominant* one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.exists_root_Pt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.exists_root_Pt","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L310-L320","doc":"`P_t` has a real root strictly between `2.16108` and `2.16109`\n(numerically `t* = 2.161083128024812632…`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.continuous_Pt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.continuous_Pt","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L306-L308","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Qy_utilde_sq_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Qy_utilde_sq_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L297-L302","doc":"**The headline algebraicity statement.** If `t > 1` is a root of `P_t`, then\n`ũ(t)²` is a root of the degree-12 polynomial `Q`. Applied to `t = t*` this is the\naudit's \"`ρ²` is algebraic of degree 12\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Qy_div_eq_zero_of_Pt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Qy_div_eq_zero_of_Pt","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L286-L293","doc":"**The transfer, over a field:** if `t ≠ 0` is a root of `P_t`, then\n`(t−2)²(t²−1)/t²` is a root of `Q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Pt_tOf_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Pt_tOf_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L280-L284","doc":"A root of `P_q` gives a root of `P_t` at `t = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Pt_tOf_mul_pow_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Pt_tOf_mul_pow_eq","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L272-L278","doc":"**`P_t` and `P_q` are the same object in the two coordinates:**\n`q¹²·P_t(q + q⁻¹) = P_q(q)·P_q(−q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.QyHom_eq_Qy_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.QyHom_eq_Qy_div","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L267-L270","doc":"`Q_hom(Y, Z) = Z¹²·Q(Y/Z)` for `Z ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.QyHom_utilde_eq_Pt_mul_Ct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.QyHom_utilde_eq_Pt_mul_Ct","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L253-L259","doc":"**The transfer identity in `ℤ[t]`:** `Q_hom((t−2)²(t²−1), t²) = P_t(t)·C(t)`.\nThis is the whole algebraic content of \"`ρ²` is a root of `Q` because `t*` is a root\nof `P_t`\" — an exact degree-48 factorisation, with the degree-36 cofactor `C` explicit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Ct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Ct","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L237-L250","doc":"The explicit degree-36 cofactor `C` in `Q_hom((t−2)²(t²−1), t²) = P_t(t)·C(t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.QyHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.QyHom","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L228-L235","doc":"The homogenisation `Q_hom(Y, Z) = Z¹²·Q(Y/Z)` of `Q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Qy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Qy","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L221-L226","doc":"`Q(y) = 54289y¹² − 3911138y¹¹ + … + 473344` — the degree-12 polynomial annihilating `ρ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Pt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Pt","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L216-L219","doc":"`P_t(t) = t¹² − 24t¹⁰ + 234t⁸ − 1208t⁶ + 3529t⁴ − 5572t² + 3728` — the minimal\npolynomial of `t* = q* + 1/q*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Pq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.Pq","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L210-L214","doc":"`P_q(q) = q¹² + 2q¹¹ − 4q¹⁰ − 8q⁹ + 6q⁸ + 16q⁷ − 10q⁶ − 16q⁵ + 6q⁴ + 8q³ − 4q² − 2q + 1`\n— the irreducible degree-12 factor of the `Δ_net` numerator whose real root `> 1` is `q*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde_sq","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L196-L202","doc":"`ũ(t)² = (t−2)²(t²−1)/t²` — the square is rational in `t`, which is what makes\nthe radius algebraic of degree ≤ 12. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde_at_cbrt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde_at_cbrt_two","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L188-L194","doc":"**The fold value in closed form:** `ũ(2^{1/3}) = −(2^{2/3} − 1)^{3/2}`\n(numerically `−0.4501964644…`, row 3 of the `|ũ|` singularity inventory). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde_at_fold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde_at_fold","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L165-L172","doc":"**The critical value at the fold.** At a fold point (`t³ = 2`, `t > 1`) the value\nof `ũ` is `−(t² − 1)^{3/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.deriv_utilde_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.deriv_utilde_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L152-L163","doc":"**The fold.** On `t > 1` the only critical point of `ũ` is `t³ = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.hasDerivAt_utilde","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.hasDerivAt_utilde","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L131-L150","doc":"**The derivative of `ũ` in the clean coordinate:** `dũ/dt = (t³ − 2)/(t²√(t² − 1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.utilde","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L128-L129","doc":"`ũ` as a function of the bar-even coordinate `t`: `ũ(t) = (t − 2)·√(t² − 1)/t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.sqrt_quartic_div_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.sqrt_quartic_div_eq","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L110-L122","doc":"**Second exact coordinate identity, archimedean form:**\n`√(q⁴ + q² + 1)/(q² + 1) = √(t² − 1)/t` for `q > 0`, `t = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf_pos","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L108-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.two_le_tOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.two_le_tOf","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L101-L106","doc":"`t = q + q⁻¹ ≥ 2` for `q > 0` (AM–GM, via `(q−1)²/q ≥ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf_sq_sub_one_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf_sq_sub_one_mul","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L88-L93","doc":"**Second exact coordinate identity, algebraic form:** `(t² − 1)·q² = q⁴ + q² + 1`.\nThis is the identity behind `√(q⁴+q²+1)/(q²+1) = √(t²−1)/t`; over a generic field\nthere is no `√`, so the content is exactly this polynomial relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf_mul","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L84-L86","doc":"`t·q = q² + 1`: the denominator of the second coordinate identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.sq_sub_one_div_eq_tOf_sub_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.sq_sub_one_div_eq_tOf_sub_two","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L77-L82","doc":"**First exact coordinate identity:** `(q−1)²/q = t − 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf_inv","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L74-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.tOf","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderRadiusAlgebraicity.lean#L71-L72","doc":"The bar-symmetric coordinate `t = q + q⁻¹`. Invariant under `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}